; The contract of the test runner: a green test step must show that the cram
; tests executed, and a test that was not meant to run must not be reported
; as one that ran. The runner is a script rather than a library, so the test
; runs it against a throw-away tree it writes itself, with a stand-in for the
; dune command: no dune runs here, nothing is built, and every case stops at
; the runner's own bookkeeping.
;
; The corpus smoke test is here for the same reason: it is a script, and its
; contract is what a binary that did not answer must never pass. Its own test
; runs it against stand-ins for the server, so no binary and no corpus are
; needed.
;
; The release scripts are tested the same way and for the same reason: each
; one is a script whose contract is its output and its status, and none of
; them needs a build, a network or a container to be exercised. check-linked.t
; writes its own stand-ins for `otool` and `ldd`, and the two checksum tests
; work in throw-away directories, so these tests run on any host and in every
; `make test`; the release build itself is not part of `ci` (docs/release.md).

(cram
 (deps
  ../../scripts/runtest.sh
  ../../scripts/corpus-smoke.sh
  ../../scripts/check-linked.sh
  ../../scripts/release-checksums.sh
  ../../scripts/release-assets.sh))
